1. WebF  (alternative rendering engine for JS plugin pages, native platforms)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
License: GNU General Public License v3.0 only (GPL-3.0-only)
Upstream: https://github.com/openwebf/webf

WebF is a self-contained W3C-compatible web runtime (custom rendering engine
plus QuickJS) that renders into the Flutter pipeline. It is used as an
alternative to the system WebView for JS plugin pages on native platforms.
It is NOT used on the Web target, which WebF does not support.

Licensing notes:
- WebF's LICENSE is the standard GPLv3 text plus an appended "OpenWebF
  Enterprise Exception". That exception is an additional permission under
  GPLv3 section 7 that applies ONLY to current enterprise or professional
  subscribers who have signed the OpenWebF Software Agreement. This project
  is not such a subscriber, so the exception does not apply here.
- There is NO LGPL-style linking exception. Distributing a binary that links
  WebF therefore places the entire combined work under GPL-3.0. See the
  "DISTRIBUTION LICENSE" section above.
- WebF ships prebuilt native libraries (libwebf.so / .dylib / .dll) which are
  bundled into our binaries by the standard Flutter plugin mechanism.

